{"id": "tea:amanaska:1.topic.laya", "source": "src:amanaska", "location": {"ref": "1.topic.laya"}, "paraphrase": "The (later) first chapter teaches layayoga through fixing attention on various places and objects and the śāmbhavī-like gaze, as a means to the mindless state.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U28-hatha-texts"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A10", "D"], "notes": "Topic-level locator: exact chapter/verse not recalled (to be supplied in Phase D).", "concepts": ["cpt:laya-natha"], "practices": ["prc:sambhavi-mudra"], "speaker": "Īśvara", "addressee": "Vāmadeva", "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U28-hatha-texts"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:amanaska:2.topic.critique", "source": "src:amanaska", "location": {"ref": "2.topic.critique"}, "paraphrase": "Breath-control, the practice of mudrās and bandhas, mantra-repetition, meditation on objects, pilgrimage, ritual and scriptural study are laborious; they do not bring the mindless state and may cause pain or disease; the wise do not resort to them.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["meditation"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["dispute", "practice"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U28-hatha-texts"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A10", "D"], "notes": "Topic-level locator: exact chapter/verse not recalled (to be supplied in Phase D). Content recalled from J. Birch's edition and studies (moderate).", "disputes": ["dsp:amanaska-critique-of-hatha", "dsp:hatha-vs-raja"], "concepts": ["cpt:taraka-amanaska"], "speaker": "Īśvara", "addressee": "Vāmadeva", "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U28-hatha-texts"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:amanaska:2.topic.effortless", "source": "src:amanaska", "location": {"ref": "2.topic.effortless"}, "paraphrase": "The mindless state (amanaska) arises without effort through the grace of the guru and a gaze that rests on no object; then the breath ceases of itself, the body becomes still, and the yogin is liberated while living.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "teacher-transmission", "karma-liberation"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U28-hatha-texts"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A10", "D"], "notes": "Topic-level locator: exact chapter/verse not recalled (to be supplied in Phase D).", "concepts": ["cpt:taraka-amanaska", "cpt:guru-in-hatha", "cpt:jivanmukti", "cpt:unmani"], "terms": ["trm:amanaska"], "disputes": ["dsp:kundalini-effort-grace"], "speaker": "Īśvara", "addressee": "Vāmadeva", "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U28-hatha-texts"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:amanaska:2.topic.signs", "source": "src:amanaska", "location": {"ref": "2.topic.signs"}, "paraphrase": "Signs of the mindless state are described: the body becomes still as a log, sense-objects are not grasped, the breath stops, and the mind neither sleeps nor wakes.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["powers-experiences"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U28-hatha-texts"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A10", "D"], "notes": "Topic-level locator: exact chapter/verse not recalled (to be supplied in Phase D).", "concepts": ["cpt:taraka-amanaska"], "speaker": "Īśvara", "addressee": "Vāmadeva", "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U28-hatha-texts"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
